{:edb/db-before-t 2460 :edb/db-after-t 2461 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535773 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:56:16.041Z" 13194139535773 true] [17592186119748 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365436 13194139535773 true] [17592186119748 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365463 13194139535773 true] [17592186119749 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365443 13194139535773 true] [17592186119749 1020 #edb/ref 17592186365456 13194139535773 true] [17592186120459 1017 #edb/ref 17592186119229 13194139535773 false] [17592186120459 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365450 13194139535773 true] [17592186120459 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535773 true] [17592186120459 1100 "Let $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}}$ be a basis of $R^{2}$ and $[x]_{B} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$. What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C = {c_{1}, c_{2}}$, where $c_{1} = b_{1} - 2b_{2}$ and $c_{2} = b_{1} + b_{2}$?" 13194139535773 false] [17592186120459 1100 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}?$" 13194139535773 true] [17592186120459 1145 "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $2$ and adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=3{b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2})-2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2})-3(-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{2}+{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365436 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365437 13194139535773 true] [17592186365436 1089 "q-112656" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365436 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535773 true] [17592186365436 1100 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365436 1113 #uuid "87dc3639-1852-54d3-8e2c-b2da8625e8b8" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365436 1145 "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365438 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365439 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365440 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365441 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365442 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1041 "selection" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365439 13194139535773 true] [17592186365437 1110 #uuid "5b1fd8ed-0b8f-5bb7-aa4a-00c7a1c964e8" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365438 1034 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535773 true] [17592186365438 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535773 true] [17592186365438 1111 